' =========================================================================
' widgets/label.dbas — Label widget (per-kind module).
'
' A Label is the simplest widget: static, non-interactive text. It has no
' runtime state, no keyboard/mouse handling, and no codegen branch of its
' own (the generated Update/View fold it into the shared "static text via
' widgetVisibleText" and "_ = key" no-op groups). So this module only owns
' two of the eight dispatch points:
'
'   A  labelDefault      — defaultWidget() defaults
'   B  labelVisibleText  — single-line design-time + runtime preview
'
' This is the pilot's warm-up extraction: it validates the per-widget
' file + INCLUDE + thin-router pattern with the smallest possible blast
' radius before the codegen-bearing kinds (Button, TabStrip) follow.
' =========================================================================

' A — defaults. The caller (defaultWidget) has already set Kind/W/H to the
' generic defaults (W=12, H=1); we override only what Label needs.
FUNCTION labelDefault(w AS DesignWidget) AS DesignWidget
    w.Text = "Label"
    w.W = 10
    RETURN w
END FUNCTION

' B — single-line preview. A Label just shows its Text verbatim.
FUNCTION labelVisibleText(w AS DesignWidget) AS STRING
    RETURN w.Text
END FUNCTION
